M1 (scripts/stack-ready.mjs members) The signal notes the newest tip of every member with started === true, and started is hasHeadEvidence: any push. A member that never ran stack-ready (only a WIP start push, or a fix pushed mid-rework) is noted as READY when the group's last card signals, so reviewers are woken for its WIP. d7 shows it: card-one never ran stack-ready and is noted. Under the push-first rule (#C1065, and Boardsmith's habit today) every member is started from its first edit, so the card's Why ("or every start push wakes a reviewer") still fails for grouped cards. Fix: note only heads the builder declared READY. When stack-ready answers "waiting for its group" or "more queued", it writes a waiting note on HEAD (its own ref, which the probe does not read as a signal). The final signal then notes a member's head only if that exact head carries a waiting note. Optionally, the batch wait also counts a member as built only with one. Tests: a member with only a start push is not noted and stays held; a member whose waiting head was followed by a WIP push is not noted; d5's two-branch case (both ran stack-ready) unheld.

